{{fbdoc item="title" value="gmp, The GNU Multiple Precision Arithmetic Library"}}----
Free library for arbitrary precision arithmetic, operating on signed integers, rational numbers, and floating point numbers.

Website: https://www.gmplib.org
Platforms supported: ""Win32"", ""Win64"", Linux, FreeBSD, Haiku
Headers to include: gmp.bi
Header version: 6.0.0

Haiku R1 beta 6 amd64: `examples/manual/libraries/gmp.bas` compiled and ran
with FreeBASIC 1.20.4-3 against HaikuPorts GMP 6.3.0, computing `2^65536`.

{{fbdoc item="section" value="Native types and ownership"}}
	The Win64 SDK uses 64-bit ##mp_limb_t## values while C ##long## remains 32-bit. ##mp_bitcnt_t##, ##mp_size_t## and ##mp_exp_t## keep their C widths. Use the binding's named types for limb pointers and low-level calls; FreeBASIC ##Integer## is not a general replacement for a C type.

	##mpz_get_str(0, ...)## allocates through GMP's current allocator. Release such a string through the corresponding registered GMP free function, obtained with ##mp_get_memory_functions##. The example supplies a FreeBASIC-owned buffer instead, sized by ##mpz_sizeinbase## plus two bytes for a sign and terminating zero, and releases it with ##Deallocate##. Release initialized number internals with ##mpz_clear## before freeing the caller's number buffer.

	The installed GMP 6.3.0 SDK has been checked against native C layouts and actual high-bit limb arguments and carry returns on Win32 and Win64, with both FreeBASIC backends. The decimal example's complete 19,729-digit result is checked independently.

{{fbdoc item="ex"}}
{{fbdoc item="filename" value="examples/manual/libraries/gmp.bas"}}%%(freebasic)
'' examples/manual/libraries/gmp.bas
''
'' Example extracted from the FreeBASIC Manual
'' from topic 'gmp, The GNU Multiple Precision Arithmetic Library'
'' Purpose: Compute and print 2^65536 through the native GMP library.
'' Responsibilities: Own the number buffer and decimal output storage.
'' This example contains no custom GMP allocator or limb arithmetic.
''
'' See Also: https://www.freebasic.net/wiki/wikka.php?wakka=ExtLibgmp
'' --------
''
'' Ownership:
''
'' The example owns the __mpz_struct buffer allocated for bignum and the
'' output string supplied to mpz_get_str().  Each is released on its matching
'' successful allocation path.

#include Once "gmp.bi"

Dim As Integer status = 0
Dim As mpz_ptr bignum = Allocate(SizeOf(__mpz_struct))
If bignum = 0 Then
	Print "Unable to allocate the GMP number."
	status = 1
Else
	mpz_init_set_si(bignum, 2)
	mpz_pow_ui(bignum, bignum, 65536)

	Print "2^65536 = ";
	' GMP can use a custom allocator. Supply our own output buffer so that
	' Deallocate() never receives memory owned by the library's allocator.
	' Two extra bytes cover a possible sign and the terminating zero.
	Dim As UInteger digits = mpz_sizeinbase(bignum, 10)
	Dim As ZString Ptr s
	If digits > 0 AndAlso digits <= CUInt(-1) - 2 Then s = Allocate(digits + 2)
	If s <> 0 Then
		If mpz_get_str(s, 10, bignum) <> 0 Then
			Print *s;
		Else
			Print "<conversion failed>";
			status = 1
		End If
		Deallocate(s)
		s = 0
	Else
		Print "<output allocation failed>";
		status = 1
	End If
	Print

	mpz_clear(bignum)
	Deallocate(bignum)
	bignum = 0
End If

End status
'' end of examples/manual/libraries/gmp.bas
%%

